{"name":"Bazaar","hex":"#8f7777","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bazaar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marketplace, particularly in the Middle East and South Asia, and often covered with shops and stalls.","A shop selling articles that are either exotic or eclectic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bazaar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bazaar","blocks":[{"text":"A bazaar or souk is a marketplace consisting of multiple small stalls or shops, especially in West Asia, North Africa, the Balkans, Central Asia, and South Asia. They are traditionally located in vaulted or covered streets that have doors on each end and served as a city's central marketplace."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Turkey_%2868742801%29.jpeg/330px-Turkey_%2868742801%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bazaar","wikidata":"Q219760"},{"title":"Bazaar (1982 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Bazaar (transl. Market) is a 1982 Indian drama film directed by Sagar Sarhadi and starring Naseeruddin Shah, Farooq Shaikh, Smita Patil and Supriya Pathak. The film set in Hyderabad, India, highlights the issue of bride buying in India, through the tragedy of a young girl being sold by needy parents to affluent expatriate Indians in the Gulf."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Bazaar_1982_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bazaar_(1982_film)","wikidata":"Q4875084"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Sanandaj_Bazaar.jpg/500px-Sanandaj_Bazaar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Sanandaj_Bazaar.jpg/1280px-Sanandaj_Bazaar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":